This sliding window keeps characters unique by moving its left boundary past a duplicate, never backward. Call solve(s) directly; it returns the length and handles an empty string by returning 0.

```javascript
function solve(s) {
  const lastSeen = new Map();
  let left = 0;
  let right = 0;
  let best = 0;

  for (const char of s) {
    if (lastSeen.has(char)) {
      left = Math.max(left, lastSeen.get(char) + 1);
    }
    lastSeen.set(char, right);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
    right++;
  }

  return best;
}
```

Time: O(n). Space: O(k), where k is the number of distinct characters. Characters are counted as Unicode code points.

