Use bottom-up dynamic programming to find the minimum coins for each total. Call solve(coins, amount) directly; zero amount returns 0, and an unreachable amount returns -1.

```javascript
function solve(coins, amount) {
  const dp = new Array(amount + 1).fill(Infinity);
  dp[0] = 0;

  for (let total = 1; total <= amount; total++) {
    for (const coin of coins) {
      if (coin <= total) {
        dp[total] = Math.min(dp[total], dp[total - coin] + 1);
      }
    }
  }

  return dp[amount] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[amount];
}
```

Time: O(amount × coins.length). Auxiliary space: O(amount).

